### ============================================================================
### Notes
### ============================================================================
#
# API Versioning: All endpoints use v1 by default (/api/v1/...)
#
# Authentication:
# - Most endpoints require JWT authentication via Bearer token
# - Register a user first, then login to get JWT and refresh tokens
# - Update jwt_token and refresh_token variables after login
#
# OAuth Authentication (Social Login):
# - Supported providers: Google, GitHub
# - Two flows available:
#   1. ID Token flow (mobile/SPA): POST /auth/oauth/login with provider token
#   2. Authorization Code flow (web): GET /auth/oauth/{provider}/authorize → callback
# - OAuth users are auto-created on first login
# - Link/unlink OAuth to existing account: POST/DELETE /auth/oauth/link
# - Configure credentials in .env: OAUTH__Google__ClientId, OAUTH__GitHub__ClientId, etc.
#
# User Management:
# - Update user endpoint (PUT /users/{id}) supports optional password change
# - To change password, provide: currentPassword, newPassword, confirmNewPassword
# - Password requirements: min 8 chars, 1 uppercase, 1 lowercase, 1 digit
# - Without password fields, only username and email are updated
#
# Docker URLs:
# - API: http://localhost:8080
# - Database: localhost:5432
# - pgAdmin: http://localhost:5050 (login: admin at admin.com / admin)
#
# Local Development URLs:
# - HTTP: http://localhost:5242
# - HTTPS: https://localhost:7095
# - Swagger: http://localhost:5242/swagger (Development only)
#
# Pagination:
# - Address endpoint supports pagination with ?page=1&perPage=10 (or pageSize=10)
# - Returns Laravel-compatible format with data, links, and meta
# - Optional sorting: ?sortBy=city&desc=true (or updatedat, isprimary)
#
# Address Management:
# - Many-to-many relationship: addresses can be shared between users
# - Each user has independent isPrimary flag for their addresses
# - Setting isPrimary=true auto-resets other addresses for that user
# - Database uses Laravel naming convention: address_user pivot table
#
# Address Types (Updated to Ukrainian):
# - ID 1: "Квартира" (Багатоквартирний будинок у місті)
# - ID 2: "Приватний будинок" (Окрема садиба або дача)
# - ID 3: "Офіс" (Комерційне або офісне приміщення)
#
# Regions:
# - 26 Ukrainian regions available (області України)
# - Use GET /api/v1/region to get full list with IDs
#
# Meters (Лічильники):
# - Full CRUD operations for utility meters
# - Supports photo upload (multipart/form-data)
# - Fields: AddressId, UtilityTypeId, Name, SerialNumber, ModelName, Location
# - Additional: InstallationDate, InitialReading, ServiceProviderId, Notes, IsActive
# - Utility Types: 1=Електроенергія, 2=Газ, 3=Холодна вода, 4=Гаряча вода, 5=Опалення
# - Photos saved to /uploads/meters/ directory
# - Get meters by address: GET /api/v1/meter/address/{addressId}
# - Get only active meters: GET /api/v1/meter/active
#
# Service Providers (Провайдери послуг):
# - New entity for utility service providers
# - Linked to meters via ServiceProviderId
# - Stores provider contact information (name, phone, email, website)
#
# Batch Meter Readings (Масове внесення показників):
# - Submit multiple meter readings at once: POST /api/v1/meter-readings/batch
# - Supports photo uploads for each meter (match by filename: photo_{meterId}.jpg)
# - Photos are automatically processed (optimized + thumbnail versions)
# - Automatic consumption calculation (current - previous reading)
# - Dynamic cost calculation based on effective tariffs
# - Validates: current >= previous, no duplicates on same date
# - Returns detailed calculations with tariff breakdown
# - Atomic transactions: all readings saved together or none
# - Get readings by address: GET /api/v1/meter-readings/address/{addressId}
# - Optional date range filtering: ?from=...&to=...
# - Response includes: consumption, baseRate, serviceFee, totalCost per meter
# - Get photos: /meter-readings/photos/{id}/optimized or /thumbnail
# - Supports HEIC/HEIF, JPEG, PNG formats
# - See docs/BATCH_METER_READINGS_API.md for full documentation
#
# CORS:
# - Configured to allow origins from environment variable
# - Docker: allows all origins (*)
# - Local: configure in .env file
